{#- The site's accessibility statement, which Israeli law and the Technion
    require (docs/research/compliance-research.md, A3 and A4). Every feature
    listed is built into the pages: the site has no overlay or toolbar widget. #}
<div class="page wrap text-page">
  <p>ATLAS Lab wants everyone to be able to use this website, including people with disabilities.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="standard">
    <h2 id="standard">Standard</h2>
    <p>This site aims to meet Israeli Standard 5568 and the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="features">
    <h2 id="features">Accessibility features</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every page opens with a skip link that leads straight to the main content.</li>
      <li>Every page can be used with the keyboard alone, and the element in focus is clearly marked.</li>
      <li>Every page has landmarks, one main heading, and the headings under it in order, for screen readers.</li>
      <li>Every image that carries meaning has a text alternative.</li>
      <li>Text has a contrast of at least 4.5:1 against its background.</li>
      <li>Pages fit a screen as narrow as 320 pixels, and can be zoomed to 400%, with no sideways scrolling.</li>
      <li>Animation is turned off when your system asks for reduced motion.</li>
      <li>Every page reads in full with JavaScript turned off.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These features are part of the pages themselves. The site has no accessibility toolbar or overlay; to enlarge the text, use your browser's zoom.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="limitations">
    <h2 id="limitations">Known limitations</h2>
    <p>Papers, recordings and other pages that this site links to are published by others, and may not be accessible. A recording of a talk may have no captions.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="report">
    <h2 id="report">Report a problem</h2>
    <p>If you meet a barrier on this site, or need something on it in an accessible form, write to the Lab mailbox, <a href="mailto:{{ site.mailbox }}">{{ site.mailbox }}</a>. Tell us the page and what went wrong, and we will do our best to help.</p>
